{"items":[{"str":"According to Grossberg, Nelson, and Treichler, the editors of the","dir":"ltr","width":300,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,168,649],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"influential anthology","dir":"ltr","width":95,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,635],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":false},{"str":" ","dir":"ltr","width":1,"height":0,"transform":[10,0,0,10,251,635],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":false},{"str":"Cultural Studies","dir":"ltr","width":75,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,257,635],"fontName":"g_d2896_f3","hasEOL":false},{"str":", the term “cultural studies”","dir":"ltr","width":136,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,332,635],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"covers a range of theoretical and political positions that use a variety of","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,621],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"methodologies, drawing on","dir":"ltr","width":127,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,607],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":false},{"str":" ","dir":"ltr","width":1,"height":0,"transform":[10,0,0,10,283,607],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":false},{"str":"ethnography","dir":"ltr","width":60,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,288,607],"fontName":"g_d2896_f1","hasEOL":false},{"str":", anthropology, sociology,","dir":"ltr","width":120,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,348,607],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"literature, feminism, Marxism, history, film criticism, psychoanalysis,","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,593],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"and semiotics. Cultural studies is anthropological, but unlike anthro-","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,579],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"pology, it begins with the study of postindustrial rather than preindus-","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,565],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"trial societies. It is like","dir":"ltr","width":100,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,551],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":false},{"str":" ","dir":"ltr","width":0,"height":0,"transform":[10,0,0,10,256,551],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":false},{"str":"humanism","dir":"ltr","width":49,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,259,551],"fontName":"g_d2896_f1","hasEOL":false},{"str":", but unlike traditional humanism it","dir":"ltr","width":160,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,308,551],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"rejects the distinction between so-called low culture and high culture","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,537],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"and argues that all forms of culture need to be studied in relation to a","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,523],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"given social formation (4). It is thus interdisciplinary in its approaches.","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,509],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"Cultural studies “has grown out of efforts to understand what has","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,495],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"shaped post World War II societies and cultures: industrialization,","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,481],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"modernization, urbanization, mass communication, commodification,","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,467],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":false},{"str":"","dir":"ltr","width":0,"height":0,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,453],"fontName":"g_d2896_f1","hasEOL":true},{"str":"imperialism","dir":"ltr","width":56,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,453],"fontName":"g_d2896_f1","hasEOL":false},{"str":", a global economy” (5).","dir":"ltr","width":109,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,212,453],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"I am using the concept of “popular,” with which cultural studies is","dir":"ltr","width":300,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,168,439],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"largely concerned, to talk about the everyday terrain of people without","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,425],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"being sure who the people are, that is, without deciding ahead of time","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,411],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"and once and for all who is being referred to by the term “people.” I","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,397],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"am also using it in the sense of “mass” culture, the popular cultural","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,383],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"forms produced through the medium of mass technology and com-","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,369],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"munications, as well as those forms produced on a smaller, localized","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,355],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"scale. I will continue in this work the traditional focus of cultural stud-","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,341],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"ies on the disempowered or marginalized within a dominant culture","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,327],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"and the ways struggles for power are conducted through representa-","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,313],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"tions. These groups are sometimes called subcultures (originally a","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,299],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"term used in Britain to refer to youth cultures): cultural formations","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,285],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"within the dominant culture that can be distinguished by a stance, a","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,271],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"style, an attitude, a position, and a fashion as defiant, resistant, or op-","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,257],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"positional to what is viewed as the dominant culture.","dir":"ltr","width":243,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,243],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":false},{"str":" ","dir":"ltr","width":0,"height":0,"transform":[10,0,0,10,399,243],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":false},{"str":"3","dir":"ltr","width":4,"height":7,"transform":[7,0,0,7,399,246],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":false},{"str":" ","dir":"ltr","width":0,"height":0,"transform":[7,0,0,7,403,246],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":false},{"str":"But the focus","dir":"ltr","width":62,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,406,243],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"here will also be on the ways mainstream culture reacts to, defines, and","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,229],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"represents certain subcultures.","dir":"ltr","width":135,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,215],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"What distinguishes cultural studies, above all, from other fields is","dir":"ltr","width":300,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,168,201],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"that it has a commitment to examining cultural practices from the","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,187],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"point of view of their intrication with, and within, relations of power.","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,173],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"That is where politics comes in: cultural studies is not a “politically","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,159],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"neutral” discipline. It is also a bridge between theory and material cul-","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,145],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":false},{"str":"","dir":"ltr","width":0,"height":0,"transform":[9,0,0,9,216,677],"fontName":"g_d2896_f3","hasEOL":true},{"str":"Cultural Studies, Popular Culture, and Pedagogy","dir":"ltr","width":191,"height":9,"transform":[9,0,0,9,216,677],"fontName":"g_d2896_f3","hasEOL":false},{"str":"","dir":"ltr","width":0,"height":0,"transform":[9,0,0,9,299,117],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"| 14 |","dir":"ltr","width":26,"height":9,"transform":[9,0,0,9,299,117],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":false}],"styles":{"g_d2896_f2":{"fontFamily":"serif","ascent":0.722,"descent":-0.246,"vertical":false},"g_d2896_f3":{"fontFamily":"serif","ascent":0.722,"descent":-0.246,"vertical":false},"g_d2896_f1":{"fontFamily":"serif","ascent":0.72,"descent":-0.245,"vertical":false}},"lang":null}